==Trivia==
*The word 雲泥 (''undei'') in Above & Below's Japanese name, 雲泥温泉郷 (''Undei Onsenkyō''), literally means "things that are very different" and is made up of the kanji for "cloud" (雲 ''un'') and "mud" (泥 ''dei''), thus a literal translation of the name would be "'''Hot Spring Village of Things That Are Very Different'''" or "'''Hot Spring Village of Cloud and Mud'''". This explains the English name, as above and below are antonyms of each other, with clouds being above and mud below.

